{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZrBzbwRLkQwaPZNEHUb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me create a summary:\n\n**Requirement (restated):** Add a POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that allows customers to cancel active orders and their created shipments, with idempotent and all-or-nothing semantics.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11-16): Has orderId, customerId, amount, currency but NO status field\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9-14): Has shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED enum)\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt): create, getById, list endpoints; uses ConflictException/ResourceNotFoundException for errors\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt): create, getById, list endpoints; no order status checks\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:24): No method to find shipments by orderId\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt): Centralizes error responses with ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Exceptions map to HTTP: ResourceNotFoundException→404, ConflictException→409\n- Error responses: {error: {code, message, fields}}\n- Tests use @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc, assert both status and response body structure\n- Repositories are @Autowired and cleared in @BeforeEach\n- In-memory ConcurrentHashMap persistence\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - add OrderStatus enum and status field (unavoidable: need to track order state)\n2. OrderController.kt - add cancel endpoint and update create to set ACTIVE status (unavoidable: core feature)\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - add findByOrderId method (unavoidable: needed to cancel order's shipments)\n4. ShipmentController.kt - add check for cancelled order (unavoidable: requirement)\n5. ApiError.kt - add new error codes (unavoidable: need distinct error types)\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt - add cancel tests (unavoidable: verification requirement)\n7. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - add test for cancelled order (unavoidable: verification requirement)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Order creation must set ACTIVE status to avoid backward compatibility break\n2. Cancel operation must be atomic (all shipments updated or none)\n3. Idempotency of cancel on already-cancelled order must not fail\n4. Preventing shipment creation on cancelled order must check order exists first\n\n**Open questions:** None - requirements are clear\n\nNow moving to the design phase:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED states. Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Update `create()` to initialize new orders with `status = ACTIVE`\n   - Add new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n     - Returns 404 if order not found\n     - If order is already CANCELLED, return 200 with the order (idempotent)\n     - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with new code ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and change nothing\n     - Otherwise: update order to CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, return the order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: \n   - In `create()`, after checking for duplicate shipment, check if order exists and is CANCELLED\n   - If order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with new code ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` - when cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment\n   - `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` - when trying to create shipment on cancelled order\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests:\n   - test_cancel_active_order_returns_order_and_cancels_created_shipments()\n   - test_cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_and_changes_nothing()\n   - test_cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_fails_with_409_and_changes_nothing()\n   - test_cancel_unknown_order_returns_404()\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test:\n   - test_create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_fails_with_409()\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n- Adding a service layer: Rejected because the baseline has no service layer; controllers handle logic directly\n- New OrderStatus/ShipmentStatus in separate enum file: Rejected to keep related enums with their entities\n- Checking order status in ShipmentRepository: Rejected because repositories should not know about order status; controller should check\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path - cancel ACTIVE order:*\n- POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- OrderController.cancel() calls repository.findById()\n- Finds order with status=ACTIVE\n- Gets all shipments via repository.findByOrderId()\n- Checks no shipments have status=CONFIRMED\n- Updates order: status=CANCELLED, saves\n- Updates each CREATED shipment: status=CANCELLED, saves\n- Returns 200 with cancelled order\n\n*Error case 1 - cancel already CANCELLED:*\n- Finds order with status=CANCELLED\n- Returns 200 with order unchanged (idempotent)\n\n*Error case 2 - CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel:*\n- Finds order with status=ACTIVE\n- Gets shipments, finds one with CONFIRMED\n- Throws ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED)\n- No updates occur (all-or-nothing)\n\n*Error case 3 - order not found:*\n- repository.findById() returns null\n- Throws ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n\n*Error case 4 - create shipment for cancelled order:*\n- POST /shipments with orderId of cancelled order\n- ShipmentController.create() checks for duplicate shipment\n- Calls repository.findById(orderId) on order repository (injected)\n- Finds order with status=CANCELLED\n- Throws ConflictException(ORDER_IS_CANCELLED)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest (4 new tests):\n1. Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments - verifies order becomes CANCELLED, shipments cancelled\n2. Cancel already CANCELLED order - verifies no error, order unchanged (idempotency)\n3. Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment - verifies 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged (all-or-nothing)\n4. Cancel unknown order - verifies 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\nShipmentControllerTest (1 new test):\n1. Create shipment for cancelled order - verifies 409 with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED code"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1694,"cache_read_input_tokens":21523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1694},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1857e58a-2e5a-4d53-8f8e-1eb8707eb70f","uuid":"fbac4447-70b0-4c93-9a14-0d17d2eeb8d5","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:19:49.789Z","request_id":"req_011CfZrBz7vtFUxk9twn4zLP"}
